{"name":"Dagger Falls","status":"ok","title":"Dagger Falls","pageId":9463,"html":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" dir=\"ltr\" lang=\"en\"><div class=\"dablink\" style=\"padding-left:2em;\"><i>This article is about the town. For the waterfall, see <a href=\"/wiki/Dagger_Falls_(waterfall)\" title=\"Dagger Falls (waterfall)\">Dagger Falls (waterfall)</a>.</i></div>\n<p class=\"mw-empty-elt\">\n</p><aside class=\"portable-infobox pi-background pi-border-color pi-theme-frwiki pi-layout-default type-location\" role=\"region\">\n\n<nav class=\"pi-navigation pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-font\"><a href=\"/wiki/Category:Maps_of_Dagger_Falls\" title=\"Category:Maps of Dagger Falls\">Gallery</a></nav>\n<h2 class=\"pi-item pi-item-spacing pi-title pi-secondary-background\" data-source=\"name\">Dagger Falls</h2>\n<section class=\"pi-item pi-group pi-border-color\">\n<h2 class=\"pi-item pi-header pi-secondary-font pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-background\">Geography</h2>\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"region\">\n<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Region</h3>\n<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\"><a href=\"/wiki/Daggerdale\" title=\"Daggerdale\">Daggerdale</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Dalelands\" title=\"Dalelands\">Dalelands</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/North_Faer%C3%BBn\" title=\"North Faerûn\">North Faerûn</a><sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FRCS3e-p127_1-1\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRCS3e-p127-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"size\">\n<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Size</h3>\n<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\">Large Town<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FRCS3e-p127_1-0\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRCS3e-p127-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></div>\n</div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"pi-item pi-group pi-border-color\">\n<h2 class=\"pi-item pi-header pi-secondary-font pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-background\">Society</h2>\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"races\">\n<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Races</h3>\n<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\"><table class=\"percentagetable\"><tbody><tr><td> <a href=\"/wiki/Human\" title=\"Human\">Humans</a> </td><td> 92%  </td></tr><tr><td> <a href=\"/wiki/Halfling\" title=\"Halfling\">Halflings</a> </td><td> 3%  </td></tr><tr><td> <a href=\"/wiki/Dwarf\" title=\"Dwarf\">Dwarves</a> </td><td> 2%  </td></tr><tr><td> <a href=\"/wiki/Half-orc\" title=\"Half-orc\">Half-orcs</a> </td><td> 2%  </td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"religion\">\n<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Religions</h3>\n<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\"><a href=\"/wiki/Lathander\" title=\"Lathander\">Lathander</a><sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FRCS3e-p127_1-3\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRCS3e-p127-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>, <a href=\"/wiki/Tyr\" title=\"Tyr\">Tyr</a><sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-CotSQ-p11_4-0\"><a href=\"#cite_note-CotSQ-p11-4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>4<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"alignment\">\n<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Alignments</h3>\n<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\"><table class=\"alignment-grid\" style=\"caption-side:top;\"> <tbody><tr> <td class=\"alignment-off\"><a href=\"/wiki/Lawful_good\" title=\"Lawful good\">LG</a></td> <td class=\"alignment-off\"><a href=\"/wiki/Neutral_good\" title=\"Neutral good\">NG</a></td> <td class=\"alignment-on\"><a href=\"/wiki/Chaotic_good\" title=\"Chaotic good\">CG</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td class=\"alignment-off\"><a href=\"/wiki/Lawful_neutral\" title=\"Lawful neutral\">LN</a></td> <td class=\"alignment-off\"><a href=\"/wiki/Neutral\" title=\"Neutral\">N</a></td> <td class=\"alignment-off\"><a href=\"/wiki/Chaotic_neutral\" title=\"Chaotic neutral\">CN</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td class=\"alignment-off\"><a href=\"/wiki/Lawful_evil\" title=\"Lawful evil\">LE</a></td> <td class=\"alignment-off\"><a href=\"/wiki/Neutral_evil\" title=\"Neutral evil\">NE</a></td> <td class=\"alignment-off\"><a href=\"/wiki/Chaotic_evil\" title=\"Chaotic evil\">CE</a></td> </tr></tbody></table></div>\n</div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"pi-item pi-group pi-border-color\">\n<h2 class=\"pi-item pi-header pi-secondary-font pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-background\">Politics</h2>\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"government\">\n<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Type</h3>\n<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\">Lordship/Constabulary</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"rulertype\">\n<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Ruler's type</h3>\n<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\">Lord/Constable</div>\n</div>\n</section>\n<h2 class=\"pi-item pi-header pi-secondary-font pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-background\">History</h2>\n<section class=\"pi-item pi-group pi-border-color\">\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"population1\">\n<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Population</h3>\n<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\">800<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-VGttD-79_2-0\"><a href=\"#cite_note-VGttD-79-2\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>2<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> in <a href=\"/wiki/1369_DR\" title=\"1369 DR\">1369 DR</a><br/>2,804<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FRCS3e-p127_1-2\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRCS3e-p127-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> in <a href=\"/wiki/1372_DR\" title=\"1372 DR\">1372 DR</a><br/>2,000<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-D.B_3-0\"><a href=\"#cite_note-D.B-3\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>3<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> in <a href=\"/wiki/1480_DR\" title=\"1480 DR\">1480 DR</a></div>\n</div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"pi-item pi-group pi-border-color\">\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"ruler1\">\n<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Lord/Constable</h3>\n<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\"><a href=\"/wiki/Morn\" title=\"Morn\">The Morn family</a><br/><a href=\"/wiki/Malyk\" title=\"Malyk\">Malyk</a> became puppet-ruler in <a href=\"/wiki/1336_DR\" title=\"1336 DR\">1336 DR</a><br/><a href=\"/wiki/Tren_Noemfor\" title=\"Tren Noemfor\">Tren Noemfor</a> became constable in <a href=\"/wiki/1353_DR\" title=\"1353 DR\">1353 DR</a><br/><span class=\"new\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvR3V0aGJlcnRfR29sdGhhbW1tZXI/YWN0aW9uPWVkaXQmcmVkbGluaz0x\" title=\"Guthbert Golthammmer (page does not exist)\">Guthbert Golthammmer</span> took over office in <a href=\"/wiki/1368_DR\" title=\"1368 DR\">1368 DR</a><br/><a href=\"/wiki/Randal_Morn\" title=\"Randal Morn\">Randal Morn</a> reclaimed town in <a href=\"/wiki/1369_DR\" title=\"1369 DR\">1369 DR</a></div>\n</div>\n</section>\n<nav class=\"pi-navigation pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-font\"><a href=\"/wiki/Category:Inhabitants_of_Dagger_Falls\" title=\"Category:Inhabitants of Dagger Falls\">Inhabitants of  Dagger Falls</a></nav>\n<nav class=\"pi-navigation pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-font\"><a href=\"/wiki/Category:Locations_in_Dagger_Falls\" title=\"Category:Locations in Dagger Falls\">Locations in  Dagger Falls</a></nav>\n<nav class=\"pi-navigation pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-font\"><a href=\"/wiki/Category:Organizations_in_Dagger_Falls\" title=\"Category:Organizations in Dagger Falls\">Organizations in  Dagger Falls</a></nav>\n</aside>\n<p class=\"mw-empty-elt\"></p><p><b>Dagger Falls</b> was a large, stone-walled town in the <a href=\"/wiki/Daggerdale\" title=\"Daggerdale\">Daggerdale</a> region of the <a href=\"/wiki/Dalelands\" title=\"Dalelands\">Dalelands</a>. The town was situated near a steep waterfall of the same name.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FRCS3e-p127_1-4\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRCS3e-p127-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<div aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\" class=\"toc\" id=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\"><input class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" role=\"button\" style=\"display:none\" type=\"checkbox\"/><div class=\"toctitle\" dir=\"ltr\" lang=\"en\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Defenses\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Defenses</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#History\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">History</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Notable_locations\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Notable locations</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Shops\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Shops</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Inns_and_taverns\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Inns and taverns</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Temples\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Temples</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Roads\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3.4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Roads</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Natural_features\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3.5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Natural features</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Appendix\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Appendix</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Appearances\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Appearances</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Gallery\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Gallery</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#References\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">References</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Defenses\">Defenses</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a aria-label=\"Edit section: Defenses\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-action=\"edit-section\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Dagger_Falls?veaction=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Defenses\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Dagger Falls had a strong stone wall encompassing the town and whilst under the rule of <a href=\"/wiki/Zhentil_Keep\" title=\"Zhentil Keep\">Zhentil Keep</a> boasted a garrison of 100 <a href=\"/wiki/Zhentilar\" title=\"Zhentilar\">Zhentilar</a> soldiers, 200 mercenaries, and roughly 130 Dalesmen reserves.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-TD-p20_5-0\"><a href=\"#cite_note-TD-p20-5\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>5<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> Two gatehouses guarded the entrances to the town, holding 35 troops each,<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-tRoRM-10_6-0\"><a href=\"#cite_note-tRoRM-10-6\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>6<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> located by the northern forest gate and eastern river gate.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-VGttD-80_7-0\"><a href=\"#cite_note-VGttD-80-7\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>7<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"History\">History</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a aria-label=\"Edit section: History\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-action=\"edit-section\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Dagger_Falls?veaction=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: History\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The site was once used as a storage site for <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/wiki/Dwarven\" title=\"Dwarven\">dwarven</a> metals mined from the <a href=\"/wiki/Desertsmouth_Mountains\" title=\"Desertsmouth Mountains\">Desertsmouth Mountains</a> to the east.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FRCS3e-p127_1-5\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRCS3e-p127-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> As all cargo heading along the <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/wiki/River_Tesh\" title=\"River Tesh\">River Tesh</a> needed to be unloaded before the <a href=\"/wiki/Dagger_Falls_(waterfall)\" title=\"Dagger Falls (waterfall)\">Dagger Falls</a> and reloaded on the other side it wasn't long before <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/wiki/Humans\" title=\"Humans\">humans</a> and other folk began coming to the site to trade with the dwarves. It was here that dwarven fortifications for the shipments sprang up and the beginnings of the village grew.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-VGttD-80_7-1\"><a href=\"#cite_note-VGttD-80-7\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>7<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p><p>Dagger Falls had long been the seat of power for Daggerdale if only by virtue of it being the largest settlement. The <a href=\"/wiki/Morn\" title=\"Morn\">Morn</a> family ruled the dale from Dagger Falls for centuries until <a href=\"/wiki/1336_DR\" title=\"1336 DR\">1336 DR</a> when the <a href=\"/wiki/Zhentarim\" title=\"Zhentarim\">Zhentarim</a> agents deposed them.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-TD-p19_8-0\"><a href=\"#cite_note-TD-p19-8\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>8<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup><sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FRCS3e-p127_1-6\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRCS3e-p127-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p><p>The town was then primarily controlled by series of Zhentilar-nominated constables, who held it until Randal Morn's triumphant retaking of Dagger Falls in <a href=\"/wiki/1369_DR\" title=\"1369 DR\">1369 DR</a>.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FRCS3e-p127_1-7\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRCS3e-p127-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p><p>In <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/wiki/1372\" title=\"1372\">1372</a>, it still existed as a frontier town under the authority of <a href=\"/wiki/Randal_Morn\" title=\"Randal Morn\">Randal Morn</a>, Lord of Daggerdale.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FRCS3e-p127_1-8\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRCS3e-p127-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Notable_locations\">Notable locations</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a aria-label=\"Edit section: Notable locations\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-action=\"edit-section\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Dagger_Falls?veaction=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Notable locations\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<dl><dt><a href=\"/wiki/Constable%27s_Tower\" title=\"Constable's Tower\">Constable's Tower</a></dt>\n<dd>This fortified tower served as the seat of power for the town's constable,<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Dalelands-p21_9-0\"><a href=\"#cite_note-Dalelands-p21-9\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>9<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> before being afflicted by a destructive magical tempest.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FRCS3e-p127_1-9\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRCS3e-p127-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></dd></dl>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Shops\">Shops</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a aria-label=\"Edit section: Shops\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-action=\"edit-section\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Dagger_Falls?veaction=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Shops\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<dl><dt><a href=\"/wiki/Fulgath%27s_Caravan_Supplies\" title=\"Fulgath's Caravan Supplies\">Fulgath's Caravan Supplies</a></dt>\n<dd>This shop provided basic provisions and goods useful to <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/wiki/Merchant\" title=\"Merchant\">merchants</a>, albeit at a 200% markup.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Dalelands-p21_9-1\"><a href=\"#cite_note-Dalelands-p21-9\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>9<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup><sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-VGttD-p88_10-0\"><a href=\"#cite_note-VGttD-p88-10\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>10<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></dd></dl>\n<dl><dt><span class=\"new\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvTWFya2V0X1NxdWFyZV8oRGFnZ2VyX0ZhbGxzKT9hY3Rpb249ZWRpdCZyZWRsaW5rPTE=\" title=\"Market Square (Dagger Falls) (page does not exist)\">Market Square</span></dt>\n<dd>This was the town's open market area.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-VGttD-p86_11-0\"><a href=\"#cite_note-VGttD-p86-11\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>11<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></dd></dl>\n<dl><dt><a href=\"/wiki/Old_Dulwar%27s_Leatherworks\" title=\"Old Dulwar's Leatherworks\">Old Dulwar's Leatherworks</a></dt>\n<dd>This store operated as a safehouse during Randal Morn's resistance and rebellion against the Zhents.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Dalelands-p21_9-2\"><a href=\"#cite_note-Dalelands-p21-9\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>9<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup><sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-D.B_3-1\"><a href=\"#cite_note-D.B-3\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>3<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></dd></dl>\n<dl><dt><span class=\"new\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvVGh1bmQlMjdzX1dhcmVob3VzZXM/YWN0aW9uPWVkaXQmcmVkbGluaz0x\" title=\"Thund's Warehouses (page does not exist)\">Thund's Warehouses</span></dt>\n<dd><sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-VGttD-p88_10-1\"><a href=\"#cite_note-VGttD-p88-10\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>10<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></dd></dl>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Inns_and_taverns\">Inns and taverns</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a aria-label=\"Edit section: Inns and taverns\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-action=\"edit-section\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Dagger_Falls?veaction=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Inns and taverns\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<dl><dt><a href=\"/wiki/Teshford_Arms\" title=\"Teshford Arms\">Teshford Arms</a></dt>\n<dd>This low quality inn, with exorbitant prices, was run by a matronly woman named <span class=\"new\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvT2xhdmlhP2FjdGlvbj1lZGl0JnJlZGxpbms9MQ==\" title=\"Olavia (page does not exist)\">Olavia</span>.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Dalelands-p21_9-3\"><a href=\"#cite_note-Dalelands-p21-9\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>9<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup><sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-VGttD-p91_12-0\"><a href=\"#cite_note-VGttD-p91-12\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>12<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></dd></dl>\n<dl><dt><a href=\"/wiki/Broken_Dagger\" title=\"Broken Dagger\">Broken Dagger</a></dt>\n<dd>The epitome of rough-and-tumble bars whose patrons were primarily <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/wiki/Zhent\" title=\"Zhent\">Zhentish</a> soldiers and mercenaries before the rebellion.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Dalelands-p21_9-4\"><a href=\"#cite_note-Dalelands-p21-9\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>9<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup><sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-VGttD-p89_13-0\"><a href=\"#cite_note-VGttD-p89-13\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>13<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></dd></dl>\n<dl><dt><a href=\"/wiki/Red_Rock\" title=\"Red Rock\">Red Rock</a></dt>\n<dd>A ramshackled inn frequented by the country folk.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-VGttD-p90_14-0\"><a href=\"#cite_note-VGttD-p90-14\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>14<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></dd></dl>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Temples\">Temples</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a aria-label=\"Edit section: Temples\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-action=\"edit-section\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Dagger_Falls?veaction=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Temples\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<dl><dt><a href=\"/wiki/Lathander%27s_Light\" title=\"Lathander's Light\">Lathander's Light</a></dt>\n<dd>This formerly grand temple was destroyed in a fire during the war with the Zhents and rebuilt afterwards as a testament to their determination and resiliance.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FRCS3e-p127_1-10\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRCS3e-p127-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup><sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Dalelands-p21_9-5\"><a href=\"#cite_note-Dalelands-p21-9\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>9<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup><sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-VGttD-p86_11-1\"><a href=\"#cite_note-VGttD-p86-11\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>11<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></dd></dl>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Roads\">Roads</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a aria-label=\"Edit section: Roads\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-action=\"edit-section\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Dagger_Falls?veaction=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Roads\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<dl><dt><span class=\"new\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvRGFnZ2VyX0JyaWRnZT9hY3Rpb249ZWRpdCZyZWRsaW5rPTE=\" title=\"Dagger Bridge (page does not exist)\">Dagger Bridge</span></dt>\n<dd><sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-BfD-12_15-0\"><a href=\"#cite_note-BfD-12-15\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>15<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></dd>\n<dt><a href=\"/wiki/Tethyamar_Trail\" title=\"Tethyamar Trail\">Tethyamar Trail</a></dt>\n<dd>The southbound road that continued to <a href=\"/wiki/Serpentsbridge\" title=\"Serpentsbridge\">Serpentsbridge</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/Spiderhaunt_Wood\" title=\"Spiderhaunt Wood\">Spiderhaunt Woods</a>.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-VGttD-p80_16-0\"><a href=\"#cite_note-VGttD-p80-16\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>16<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></dd>\n<dt><a href=\"/wiki/Tesh_Trail\" title=\"Tesh Trail\">Tesh Trail</a></dt>\n<dd><sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-VGttD-p80_16-1\"><a href=\"#cite_note-VGttD-p80-16\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>16<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></dd></dl>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Natural_features\">Natural features</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a aria-label=\"Edit section: Natural features\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-action=\"edit-section\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Dagger_Falls?veaction=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Natural features\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<dl><dt><a href=\"/wiki/Dagger_Falls_(waterfall)\" title=\"Dagger Falls (waterfall)\">Dagger Falls</a></dt>\n<dd>The eponymous waterfall had a sheer drop and was unnavigable by boats.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FRCS3e-p127_1-11\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRCS3e-p127-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></dd></dl>\n<dl><dt><a href=\"/wiki/Eagles%27_Eyrie\" title=\"Eagles' Eyrie\">Eagles' Eyrie</a></dt>\n<dd>This rocky knoll was home to altars sacred to the <a href=\"/wiki/Clan_Brightblade\" title=\"Clan Brightblade\">Clan Brightblade</a> of <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/wiki/Dwarves\" title=\"Dwarves\">Dwarves</a>.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FRCS3e-p127_1-12\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRCS3e-p127-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup><sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-VGttD-p84_17-0\"><a href=\"#cite_note-VGttD-p84-17\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>17<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></dd></dl>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Appendix\">Appendix</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a aria-label=\"Edit section: Appendix\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-action=\"edit-section\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Dagger_Falls?veaction=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Appendix\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Appearances\">Appearances</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a aria-label=\"Edit section: Appearances\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-action=\"edit-section\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Dagger_Falls?veaction=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Appearances\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<dl><dd><dl><dt>Adventures</dt>\n<dd><i><a href=\"/wiki/The_Return_of_Randal_Morn\" title=\"The Return of Randal Morn\">The Return of Randal Morn</a></i> • <i><a href=\"/wiki/Doom_of_Daggerdale\" title=\"Doom of Daggerdale\">Doom of Daggerdale</a></i></dd>\n<dt>Video Games</dt>\n<dd><i><a href=\"/wiki/Curse_of_the_Azure_Bonds_(game)\" title=\"Curse of the Azure Bonds (game)\">Curse of the Azure Bonds</a></i></dd></dl></dd></dl>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Gallery\">Gallery</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a aria-label=\"Edit section: Gallery\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-action=\"edit-section\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Dagger_Falls?veaction=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Gallery\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<div class=\"wikia-gallery wikia-gallery-caption-below wikia-gallery-position-left wikia-gallery-spacing-medium wikia-gallery-border-small wikia-gallery-captions-left wikia-gallery-caption-size-medium\" data-seq-no=\"0\" hash=\"2101f96fef68203d0bfbf62273438a43\" id=\"gallery-0\"><div class=\"wikia-gallery-caption\"></div><div class=\"wikia-gallery-item\" style=\"width:187px; \"><div class=\"lightbox-caption\" style=\"width:185px;\">2e map</div></div></div>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"References\